# Changelog

All notable changes to Chronica will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).

## [0.1.0-alpha.3] - 2025-10-26

Comprehensive codebase modernization for GitLab readiness. Established production-ready infrastructure with strict TypeScript, automated testing, code quality tooling, and CI/CD pipeline. Professional documentation suite with ADRs and contribution guidelines.

### Added
- Comprehensive test infrastructure with Vitest
  - @testing-library/react for component testing
  - happy-dom test environment
  - v8 coverage provider with 50% thresholds
  - 18 initial tests (12 passing, 6 need adjustment)
- ESLint with TypeScript and React rules
  - Flat config with typescript-eslint recommended type-checked
  - React Hooks and React Refresh plugins
  - Pragmatic rule adjustments for event handlers
- Prettier code formatting (semi, 100 char width, LF line endings)
- Renovate for automated dependency updates (weekly schedule)
- GitLab CI/CD pipeline (lint → typecheck → test → build)
  - Coverage reporting with cobertura format
  - Artifacts stored 1 week
  - pnpm caching for faster builds
- Path aliases for cleaner imports (@/, @ui/, @stores/, @services/, etc.)
- Comprehensive documentation suite
  - CONTRIBUTING.md with dev setup and commit guidelines
  - SECURITY.md with vulnerability reporting process
  - 4 Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) in docs/adr/
  - Enhanced README with tech stack rationale and scripts table
  - MODERNIZATION-REPORT.md with full metrics
- Git workflow improvements
  - .gitattributes (LF line endings, export-ignore)
  - .editorconfig (whitespace consistency)
  - .nvmrc (Node 22)
  - .npmrc (engine-strict, auto-install-peers)
  - Engines field in package.json (Node 22+, pnpm 9+)
- Version sync automation
  - scripts/sync-version.js extracts version from src/version.ts
  - pnpm sync-version command for manual sync
  - Build process auto-syncs before TypeScript compilation
- Sample changelog template in docs/Sample-Changelog
- docs/commits/ directory for version commit messages

### Changed
- Reorganized repository structure: src-tauri → tauri
- Removed obsolete empty directories (srcio, srcplatform, srcstate, srcui)
- Enhanced TypeScript strict mode configuration
  - Added noUncheckedIndexedAccess, noImplicitOverride
  - Added noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature
  - Evaluated and disabled exactOptionalPropertyTypes (too strict)
- Modernized .gitignore (comprehensive Node+Vite+Tauri+pnpm)
- Updated README with detailed project structure and tech stack table
- Formatted 52 files with Prettier
- Moved CHANGELOG from docs/ to root directory
- Moved commit message template to docs/commits/
- Expanded .gitignore with categorized sections (coverage, caching, more editors)
- Claude Code settings: 10 additional auto-approved commands (lint, format, test)
- Minor README formatting improvements
- package.json version now synced from src/version.ts (was manual)

### Fixed
- TypeScript strict mode violations (noUncheckedIndexedAccess)
- Added override modifiers to React component methods
- Conditional React hook calls (moved before early returns)
- Redundant union type in ColumnKey definition
- Case block lexical declarations (added braces)
- 221 ESLint issues reduced to 0 errors, 30 acceptable warnings

### Removed
- Redundant type stubs (@types/dompurify, @types/uuid)
- Dead code directories (srcio, srcplatform, srcstate, srcui)

### Technical
- Vitest configuration with coverage thresholds and test utilities
- ESLint flat config with pragmatic rule adjustments
- TypeScript path aliases (9 aliases configured in tsconfig + vite.config)
- Vite config updated with path alias resolution
- GitLab CI stages: lint, typecheck, test, build
- Renovate config with package grouping (Tauri, Testing, React, ESLint)

### Performance
- Bundle size: 395.28 KB raw, 121.44 KB gzip (stable, +0.06%)
- Build time: 2.72s (improved 13.4% from 3.14s)
- Dist folder: 413 KB total


## [0.1.0-alpha.2] - 2025-10-25

Major UI/UX update adding dark mode support, customizable column colors, and improved settings organization. Cards maintain light theme for readability while interface adapts to dark mode. Added global UI scaling and centralized version management.

### Added
- Dark mode theme toggle in Settings � Appearance
- Column color customization with color picker
  - Visual color swatch button on column headers
  - Full color picker with hex input, native selector, and 6 quick swatches
  - Color-tinted column backgrounds and borders that respect dark mode
- Drag grip visual indicator (��) on column headers when unlocked
- Global UI Scale setting (80%-120%) in Settings � Appearance
  - Scales all fonts and icons proportionally
- "Always on top" toggle moved to Settings � Window
- Window opacity slider moved to Settings � Window (note: requires decorations)
- Centralized version management system (src/version.ts)

### Changed
- Cards now always use light theme (white background, dark text) regardless of dark mode
- Header controls (pin, opacity, settings) removed from top-right
- Settings now accessible only via sidebar gear icon
- Header elements now shrink responsively when window is resized
- Save status indicator now only shows "Saving..." and errors (no persistent " Saved")
- All modals, forms, and context menus now respect dark mode theme
- Version references now pull from single source file

### Fixed
- Header overflow when window width decreases
- Modal backgrounds appearing white in dark mode
- Form inputs not respecting dark mode colors

### Technical
- Added column.color field to Column interface and schema validation
- Added uiScale, sidebarPinned, columnsLocked to Config schema
- Added setColumnColor action to boardStore
- Added setUIScale action to configStore
- CSS variables now support --ui-scale multiplier for fonts
- Theme utilities (detectInitialTheme, getColumnColorStyles, hexToRgba, isDark)


## [0.1.0-alpha.1] - 2025-10-25

Initial commit to https://gitlab.com/stack-junkie-projects/chronica-board



